<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis bids mostly unchanged.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis bids for hard red winter wheat were mostly unchanged and movement of wheat was very slow, grain merchandisers in the High Plains said Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It's been pretty slow going all day yesterday and today,&quot; a central Kansas dealer said.</p>
<p>Merchandisers said the balmy temperatures seen over the last five days in the central Plains were giving way to more seasonal, cooler weather. A cold snap was expected to descend on the area by Friday, when high temperatures were expected to be in the upper 20s and 30s Fahrenheit in Kansas.  </p>
